<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hemu</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1501">1501</a>–<a href="/years/1556">1556</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Hem Chandra Vikramaditya, Samrat Hem Chandra Vikramaditya</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Hemu was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> general and minister of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sur-empire">Sur Empire</a> who rose from a merchant background to command the armies of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adil-shah">Adil Shah</a> Suri. After winning many battles against Afghan rivals and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughals</a>, he took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a> in 1556 and proclaimed himself king as Vikramaditya. Weeks later he was wounded by an arrow at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-battle-of-panipat">Second Battle of Panipat</a>, captured and executed.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hemu.jpg" alt="Hemu" width="320" height="364" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 1602-03 artist · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hemu_captured_by_Akbar%27s_forces_in_1556.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
